# Configuration for docker compose. Copy to .env (gitignored) before the first run:
#
#   cp .env.example .env
#
# then append the two generated secrets, as shown in the README. Compose refuses to
# start while a password below, or either secret, is missing.

# --- Generated secrets: no defaults, on purpose ---
# Encrypts connections and variables stored in Airflow's metadata database.
# FERNET_KEY=
# Signs the tokens Airflow's components use to talk to each other.
# AIRFLOW__API_AUTH__JWT_SECRET=

# --- Passwords: fine on a laptop, change them before exposing any port ---
# They are placed inside connection URLs, so keep to letters, digits, - and _.
# Postgres only reads its password when a volume is first created; changing one
# later needs `docker compose down -v` (wipes data) or an ALTER USER.

# Pipeline database (user "wiki", database "wikipulse").
POSTGRES_PASSWORD=wiki
# Airflow metadata database (user "airflow").
AIRFLOW_DB_PASSWORD=airflow
# Airflow web UI login, http://localhost:8082
_AIRFLOW_WWW_USER_USERNAME=airflow
_AIRFLOW_WWW_USER_PASSWORD=airflow

# --- Optional ---
# On Linux, set to your user id (id -u) so files Airflow writes to ./logs are yours.
# AIRFLOW_UID=50000
